const dictionary=[["Data group","What is provided","How it is reported / caveat"],["Identity and timing","Project name, source-specific Project ID, utility/PTO, report period, observation date, status, approval cycle/year.",`Filter Project ID to see a project's retained report history, then sort Observation date. IDs are stable within their source stream; CAISO annual-plan, Board-presentation, planning-report, TDF, utility TPR, and primary-project sources are separate systems and should not be joined without a documented crosswalk. The 2009 proposal review links only ${proposalCrosswalkReview.linked} of ${proposalCrosswalkReview.reviewed_proposals} proposals; ${proposalCrosswalkReview.unresolved} remain intentionally unlinked.`],["Cost","Reported and initial costs in nominal $M; a dollar year beside each cost; and selected-year CPI-U comparison costs/differences.","Utility TPR source costs are in $000 and are converted to $M. CAISO plan ranges display as midpoints, '<' values as their stated ceiling, and $0 as reported; the September 2007 Tehachapi $1.8B is an unallocated aggregate. The Tehachapi CPUC/SCE lifecycle rows use a stated source dollar year where the source provides one; other sources use a report-year proxy. Exact source text is retained in Source locator."],["Schedule","Initial and reported/actual in-service dates; schedule shift where both date values are supplied.","The January Board presentation and September 2007 Tehachapi report preserve planned component ISDs, not actual completion. The Tehachapi lifecycle adds CPUC and SCE status milestones, including SCE’s segment-completion timeline. The 2008, 2010/11, and 2011/12–2025/26 final plans provide planned, target, or expected ISDs for cited project rows. Status tables record completed, cancelled, and some source-described replacements/re-scopes. The 2025/26 recommendation tables do not report an ISD, so their schedule field is blank. CAISO TDF has schedule/status observations. Utility TPR adds original and current/actual dates when reported."],["Path and size","Location, narrative path/scope, line length, voltage, and capacity.","The September 2007 Tehachapi report provides Appendix G Table 1 component scope/size where stated; the primary Tehachapi lifecycle adds CPUC routing/undergrounding and SCE completion evidence. Annual-plan rows carry only fields reported in their table: 2008 has PG&E scope/purpose; 2010/11 onward new-needed rows have service area. Utility TPR adds most other path and size fields. A blank means the source did not report it, not zero or no change."],["Change and evidence","Change signal, eligibility, latest utility record flag, source ID, locator, direct URL, title.","Change signals are automated comparisons or reported statuses. They are research flags, not confirmation of a reroute, cancellation, or cost overrun."]];
